			<title>NSF I-Corps: Explore your innovation’s potential for societal &amp; economic impact! </title>
			<description>NSF I-Corps: Explore your innovation’s potential for societal &amp; economic impact! &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Virtual and conference-based courses led by the Interior Northeast I-Corps Hub  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Could your innovative research change the world?   &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Participate in a free, month-long I-Corps Regional Course to receive expert guidance as you evaluate the market potential of your deep technology innovation. You’ll gain a d...</description>
			<fullDescription>NSF I-Corps: Explore your innovation’s potential for societal &amp; economic impact! &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Virtual and conference-based courses led by the Interior Northeast I-Corps Hub  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Could your innovative research change the world?   &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Participate in a free, month-long I-Corps Regional Course to receive expert guidance as you evaluate the market potential of your deep technology innovation. You’ll gain a deeper understanding of your field and learn valuable professional skills in the process.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The following conference courses begin online and feature funded customer discovery travel to an industry-specific event:  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;September 21 – October 21: For researchers developing battery tech innovations. Includes travel to Detroit, MI for The Battery Show. Apply by August 26. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;September 21 – October 21: For researchers developing semiconductor and microelectronics innovations. Includes travel to San Francisco, CA for SEMICON West. Apply by August 26. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;September 28 – October 28: For researchers developing medtech innovations. Includes travel to Boston, MA for The MedTech Conference. Apply by September 2.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;October 26 – November 23: For researchers developing energy storage innovations. Features travel to Las Vegas, NV for the RE+ Conference. Apply by September 30.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;December 7 – January 15: For researchers developing ag tech innovations. Features travel to Charlotte, NC for the American Farm Bureau Convention. Apply by November 4. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The following virtual courses are open to innovators in all STEM fields:  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;July 27 – August 26: For startup/incubator teams. Apply by July 8. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;September 4 – October 7: Apply by August 19. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;October 12 – November 12: Apply by September 16.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;October 19 – November 18: Apply by September 23. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;October 19 – November 18: For startup/incubator teams. Apply by September 23.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;November 11 – December 16: Apply by October 14.  &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Apply now! &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Please contact icorps@cornell.edu for any questions.  </fullDescription>
